  std::unordered_map<std::string, ObjectReference> namingMap_;
};
```

In the solution, the `BBNamingContextServer` class uses a `std::mutex` to ensure exclusive access to the naming map during `bind`, `unbind`, and `resolve` operations, thus providing thread safety for concurrent access. The `std::unordered_map` `namingMap_` is used to store the name-object reference mappings. The `bind` method associates a name with an object reference, `unbind` removes the binding for a given name, and `resolve` retrieves the object reference associated with a given name. The `std::lock_guard` is used to automatically release the lock when the method exits, ensuring proper synchronization and preventing deadlocks.

