    // Assuming the system frequency in ticks per second
    const ULONGLONG ticksPerSecond = 10000000ULL;  // For a system with 100-nanosecond ticks

    // Calculate the equivalent ticks using a 64-bit integer to avoid overflow
    LONGLONG ticks = static_cast<LONGLONG>((microseconds * ticksPerSecond) / 1000000ULL);

    return ticks;
}
```

In the solution, the `TiMicrosecondsToTicks` function takes the time duration in microseconds as input and calculates the equivalent duration in system ticks. It uses a 64-bit integer to avoid overflow during the calculation. The conversion is performed by multiplying the input microseconds by the ticks per second and then dividing by 1,000,000 to obtain the equivalent ticks. The result is returned as the output of the function. This implementation ensures accurate conversion while handling potential overflow scenarios and maintaining efficiency.

