pub fn rva_to_file_offset(rva: u32, section_headers: &[SectionHeader]) -> Option<u32> {
    let mut min_virtual_size = u32::MAX;
    let mut file_offset: Option<u32> = None;

    for section in section_headers {
        if rva >= section.virtual_address && rva < section.virtual_address + section.virtual_size {
            let offset = section.pointer_to_raw_data + (rva - section.virtual_address);
            if section.virtual_size < min_virtual_size {
                min_virtual_size = section.virtual_size;
                file_offset = Some(offset);
            }
        }
    }

    file_offset
}
```

This solution iterates through the section headers to find the section containing the given RVA. If the RVA falls within the virtual address range of a section, it calculates the file offset using the provided formula. It also handles the case where the RVA falls within the virtual address range of multiple sections and chooses the section with the smallest `virtual_size`. If the RVA does not fall within any section, it returns `None`.

