function processHighlightTokens(highlightTokens) {
  const result = {};
  highlightTokens.forEach(({ fileName, highlightToken }) => {
    if (typeof highlightToken === "string") {
      if (!result[fileName]) {
        result[fileName] = { strings: [], numbers: [], warnings: [] };
      }
      result[fileName].strings.push(highlightToken);
    } else if (typeof highlightToken === "number") {
      if (!result[fileName]) {
        result[fileName] = { strings: [], numbers: [], warnings: [] };
      }
      result[fileName].numbers.push(highlightToken);
    } else {
      result[fileName] = result[fileName] || { strings: [], numbers: [], warnings: [] };
      result[fileName].warnings.push(`The "${fileName}" file has a highlight token which is of type "${typeof highlightToken}"; this is not parsable and will be ignored.`);
    }
  });
  return result;
}
```

The `processHighlightTokens` function iterates through the array of highlight tokens, categorizing them based on their type and associating them with the corresponding file names. If the highlight token is a string or a number, it is added to the respective list in the result object. If the highlight token is of any other type, a warning message is added to the warnings list for the associated file. The function returns an object containing lists of strings and numbers associated with each file, along with any warning messages for unexpected highlight token types.

