        stackArray = new int[capacity];
        top = -1;
    }

    public void push(int val) {
        if (top == stackArray.length - 1) {
            // Stack is full, throw an exception or resize the array
            throw new IllegalStateException("Stack is full");
        }
        stackArray[++top] = val;
    }

    public int pop() {
        if (isEmpty()) {
            // Stack is empty, throw an exception or return a specific value
            throw new IllegalStateException("Stack is empty");
        }
        return stackArray[top--];
    }

    public int peek() {
        if (isEmpty()) {
            // Stack is empty, throw an exception or return a specific value
            throw new IllegalStateException("Stack is empty");
        }
        return stackArray[top];
    }

    public boolean isEmpty() {
        return top == -1;
    }
}
```

This solution provides a complete implementation of the WKRStack class with the specified operations using an array as the underlying storage. The class initializes the stack with the given capacity and supports push, pop, peek, and isEmpty operations as required.

