class Solution:
    def diameterOfBinaryTree(self, root: TreeNode) -> int:
        def calc_height(node):
            nonlocal max_diameter
            if not node:
                return 0
            left_height = calc_height(node.left)
            right_height = calc_height(node.right)
            max_diameter = max(max_diameter, left_height + right_height)
            return 1 + max(left_height, right_height)

        max_diameter = 0
        calc_height(root)
        return max_diameter
```

The `diameterOfBinaryTree` method uses a helper function `calc_height` to recursively calculate the height of each node in the binary tree. While calculating the height, it also updates the `max_diameter` variable to keep track of the maximum diameter found so far. Finally, the method returns the maximum diameter of the binary tree.

