You are tasked with implementing a unique binary search tree (BST) builder that takes an array of integers and constructs a BST with unique values. The BST should enforce uniqueness, meaning that no duplicate values are allowed in the tree.

You are given the following code snippet as a starting point:

```csharp
[Test]
public void TestBuildUnique()
{
    var node = BulkTreeBuilder<KeyNode<int>, int, int, KeyNode<int>.Driver>.BuildFrom(new[] { 1, 3, 4, 2, 5 }, Comparer<int>.Default, DuplicateHandling.EnforceUnique);
}
```

Your task is to implement the `BulkTreeBuilder` class and its associated methods to construct a unique BST from the given array of integers. The `BuildFrom` method should take the array of integers, a comparer for ordering the elements, and a duplicate handling strategy as parameters.

Your implementation should ensure that the resulting BST contains unique values and adheres to the properties of a BST, where the left subtree of a node contains only nodes with values less than the node's value, and the right subtree contains only nodes with values greater than the node's value.

Write the `BulkTreeBuilder` class and the `BuildFrom` method to achieve this functionality.

output:
```csharp
public enum DuplicateHandling
{
    EnforceUnique,
    AllowDuplicates
}

public class BulkTreeBuilder<TNode, TKey, TValue, TDriver>
    where TNode : KeyNode<TKey>
    where TDriver : IBulkTreeDriver<TNode, TKey, TValue>
{
    public static TNode BuildFrom(TValue[] values, IComparer<TValue> comparer, DuplicateHandling duplicateHandling)
    {
        if (values == null || values.Length == 0)
        {
            throw new ArgumentException("Input array cannot be null or empty.");
        }

        TDriver driver = Activator.CreateInstance<TDriver>();
        TNode root = null;

        foreach (var value in values)
        {
            if (duplicateHandling == DuplicateHandling.EnforceUnique && driver.ContainsKey(value))
            {
                throw new ArgumentException("Duplicate value found and uniqueness enforcement is enabled.");
            }

            TNode newNode = Activator.CreateInstance<TNode>();
            newNode.Key = value;

            if (root == null)
            {
                root = newNode;
            }
            else
            {
                InsertNode(root, newNode, comparer);
            }
        }

        return root;
    }

    private static void InsertNode(TNode root, TNode newNode, IComparer<TValue> comparer)
    {
        if (comparer.Compare(newNode.Key, root.Key) < 0)
        {
            if (root.Left == null)
            {
                root.Left = newNode;
            }
            else
            {
                InsertNode(root.Left, newNode, comparer);
            }
        }
        else
        {
            if (root.Right == null)
            {
                root.Right = newNode;
            }
            else
            {
                InsertNode(root.Right, newNode, comparer);
            }
        }
    }
}

public interface IBulkTreeDriver<TNode, TKey, TValue>
{
    bool ContainsKey(TValue key);
}

public class KeyNode<T> : IBulkTreeDriver<KeyNode<T>, T, T>
{
    public T Key { get; set; }
    public KeyNode<T> Left { get; set; }
    public KeyNode<T> Right { get; set; }

    public bool ContainsKey(T key)
    {
        if (EqualityComparer<T>.Default.Equals(key, Key))
        {
            return true;
        }
        else if (Comparer<T>.Default.Compare(key, Key) < 0 && Left != null)
        {
            return Left.ContainsKey(key);
        }
        else if (Comparer<T>.Default.Compare(key, Key) > 0 && Right != null)
        {
            return Right.ContainsKey(key);
        }
        return false;
    }
}
```

This solution provides a `BulkTreeBuilder` class with a `BuildFrom` method that constructs a unique BST from the given array of values. The `DuplicateHandling` enum is used to specify whether duplicate values are allowed or not. The `KeyNode` class represents the nodes of the BST and implements the `IBulkTreeDriver` interface to check for key existence. The `InsertNode` method is used to recursively insert nodes into the BST based on the comparer's ordering.

