Your task is to complete the implementation of the sorting algorithm within the `sortnet` namespace. The sorting algorithm should take a pointer to the head of the linked list as input and rearrange the elements in non-decreasing order. You should ensure that the original pointers within the linked list are updated accordingly.

Your implementation should be efficient and should not use any standard library sorting functions. You are expected to provide a solution that sorts the linked list in-place without using additional data structures.

Write a function `void sortLinkedList(Node* head)` within the `sortnet` namespace to accomplish this task. The `Node` structure for the linked list is defined as follows:

```cpp
struct Node {
    int data;
    Node* next;
};
```

output:
```cpp
// File: util.cpp
#include <sortnet/util.h>

namespace sortnet {
    void sortLinkedList(Node* head) {
        if (head == nullptr || head->next == nullptr) {
            return;  // No need to sort if the list is empty or has only one element
        }

        bool swapped;
        Node* temp;

        do {
            swapped = false;
            temp = head;

            while (temp->next != nullptr) {
                if (temp->data > temp->next->data) {
                    // Swap the data of the current and next nodes
                    int tempData = temp->data;
                    temp->data = temp->next->data;
                    temp->next->data = tempData;
                    swapped = true;
                }
                temp = temp->next;
            }
        } while (swapped);
    }
