from typing import List

def simulate_file_system(commands: List[str]) -> List[str]:
    file_system = {
        "file1",
        "file2",
        "directory1/",
        "directory1/file3",
        "directory1/file4",
        "directory2/",
        "directory2/file5"
    }

    for command in commands:
        if command.startswith("rm -rf"):
            directory = command.split(" ")[-1]
            to_remove = [item for item in file_system if item.startswith(directory)]
            file_system.difference_update(to_remove)
        elif command.startswith("rm"):
            file_system.discard(command.split(" ")[-1])

    return sorted(list(file_system))
```

The `simulate_file_system` function initializes the file system with the given files and directories. It then iterates through the commands, handling each one by removing the specified files or directories from the file system. After processing all the commands, it returns the final state of the file system as a sorted list of files and directories.

