You are tasked with implementing a simple reference-counted smart pointer in Rust. The smart pointer should support reference counting and deallocation of the underlying resource when the last reference is dropped.

Your task is to complete the implementation of the `Rc` (Reference Counted) smart pointer in Rust. The `Rc` smart pointer is a common type used for shared ownership in Rust. It allows multiple ownership of the same data by keeping track of the number of references to the data and automatically deallocating the data when the last reference is dropped.

You need to implement the following methods for the `Rc` smart pointer:
1. `new`: This method should create a new `Rc` smart pointer with the given value.
2. `clone`: This method should create a new reference to the same data, increasing the reference count.
3. `strong_count`: This method should return the current reference count of the `Rc` smart pointer.

You should use the provided code snippet as a starting point and complete the implementation of the `Rc` smart pointer.

```rust
use std::ptr::null_mut;
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};

pub struct Rc<T> {
    data: *mut T,
    ref_count: AtomicUsize,
}

impl<T> Rc<T> {
    pub fn new(data: T) -> Self {
        let boxed_data = Box::new(data);
        let data_ptr = Box::into_raw(boxed_data);
        Self {
            data: data_ptr,
            ref_count: AtomicUsize::new(1),
        }
    }

    pub fn clone(&self) -> Self {
        self.ref_count.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);
        Self {
            data: self.data,
            ref_count: self.ref_count.clone(),
        }
    }

    pub fn strong_count(&self) -> usize {
        self.ref_count.load(Ordering::Relaxed)
    }
}

impl<T> Drop for Rc<T> {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        if self.ref_count.fetch_sub(1, Ordering::Release) == 1 {
            // Last reference, deallocate the data
            unsafe {
                Box::from_raw(self.data);
            }
        }
    }
}

fn main() {
    let rc1 = Rc::new(42);
    let rc2 = rc1.clone();
    let rc3 = rc2.clone();

    assert_eq!(rc1.strong_count(), 3);
    assert_eq!(rc2.strong_count(), 3);
    assert_eq!(rc3.strong_count(), 3);
}
```

