/**
 * Encrypt and persist sensitive data.
 *
 * @param mixed $sensitive_data The sensitive data to be encrypted and persisted.
 * @param string $path_to_sensitive_data The file path where the encrypted data will be persisted.
 * @param string $key The encryption key.
 * @param string $associated_data The associated data for encryption.
 * @return void
 */
function encryptAndPersist($sensitive_data, $path_to_sensitive_data, $key, $associated_data) {
    if (!extension_loaded('sodium')) {
        throw new Exception('Sodium extension is not available. Please install the sodium extension for PHP.');
    }

    // Serialize the sensitive data
    $serialized_data = serialize($sensitive_data);

    // Encrypt the serialized data
    $nonce = random_bytes(SODIUM_CRYPTO_AEAD_AES256GCM_NPUBBYTES);
    $ciphertext = sodium_crypto_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt($serialized_data, $associated_data, $nonce, $key);

    // Write the encrypted data to the specified file
    $file_handle = fopen($path_to_sensitive_data, 'wb');
    if ($file_handle === false) {
        throw new Exception('Failed to open the file for writing.');
    }
    fwrite($file_handle, $nonce);
    fwrite($file_handle, $ciphertext);
    fclose($file_handle);
}
```

In the solution, the `encryptAndPersist` function first checks if the `sodium` extension is available. It then serializes the sensitive data, encrypts it using `sodium_crypto_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt`, and writes the encrypted data along with the nonce to the specified file path. The function also handles errors by throwing exceptions when necessary.

