public class AggregationProcessor {
    private Map<AggregationColumn, AggregationUnit> aggregationUnitMap;

    public void aggregate() throws SQLException {
        for (Map.Entry<AggregationColumn, AggregationUnit> each : aggregationUnitMap.entrySet()) {
            List<AggregationColumn> mergingAggregationColumns = mergeAggregationColumns(each.getKey());
            List<Comparable<?>> comparables = new ArrayList<>(mergingAggregationColumns.size());
            for (AggregationColumn column : mergingAggregationColumns) {
                // Perform aggregation logic for each column
            }
        }
    }

    public List<AggregationColumn> mergeAggregationColumns(AggregationColumn column) {
        List<AggregationColumn> mergedColumns = new ArrayList<>();
        mergeAggregationColumnsRecursive(column, mergedColumns);
        return mergedColumns;
    }

    private void mergeAggregationColumnsRecursive(AggregationColumn column, List<AggregationColumn> mergedColumns) {
        if (!mergedColumns.contains(column)) {
            mergedColumns.add(column);
            for (AggregationColumn derivedColumn : column.getDerivedColumns()) {
                mergeAggregationColumnsRecursive(derivedColumn, mergedColumns);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

The `mergeAggregationColumns` method recursively merges the given aggregation column and its derived columns into a list of all columns to be included in the aggregation process. It ensures that each column and its derived columns are added only once to the merged list, preventing duplication. This solution effectively handles the merging of aggregation columns and their derived columns, providing a comprehensive aggregation algorithm for the database system.

