            max_length = max(max_length, current_length)
            current_length = 1

    return max(max_length, current_length)
```

The `longestContiguousSubarray` function iterates through the input list of temperatures, keeping track of the current length of contiguous subarray where the temperature difference is at most 1. It updates the `max_length` whenever a longer contiguous subarray is found. Finally, it returns the maximum length found.

