1. A constructor that takes in an array of currency exchange rates as a parameter.
2. A method to convert an amount from one currency to another.
3. A method to retrieve the list of supported currencies.
4. A method to retrieve the base currency used for conversion.

Your task is to complete the CurrencyConverter class according to the given specifications.

```php
<?php
class CurrencyConverter
{
    private $exchangeRates;
    private $baseCurrency;

    /**
     * CurrencyConverter constructor.
     * @param array $exchangeRates
     * @param string $baseCurrency
     */
    public function __construct(array $exchangeRates, string $baseCurrency)
    {
        $this->exchangeRates = $exchangeRates;
        $this->baseCurrency = $baseCurrency;
    }

    /**
     * Convert an amount from one currency to another.
     * @param float $amount
     * @param string $fromCurrency
     * @param string $toCurrency
     * @return float
     */
    public function convert(float $amount, string $fromCurrency, string $toCurrency): float
    {
        if ($fromCurrency === $this->baseCurrency) {
            return $amount * $this->exchangeRates[$toCurrency];
        } elseif ($toCurrency === $this->baseCurrency) {
            return $amount / $this->exchangeRates[$fromCurrency];
        } else {
            $amountInBaseCurrency = $amount / $this->exchangeRates[$fromCurrency];
            return $amountInBaseCurrency * $this->exchangeRates[$toCurrency];
        }
    }

    /**
     * Get the list of supported currencies.
     * @return array
     */
    public function getSupportedCurrencies(): array
    {
        return array_keys($this->exchangeRates);
    }

    /**
     * Get the base currency used for conversion.
     * @return string
     */
    public function getBaseCurrency(): string
    {
        return $this->baseCurrency;
    }
}
?>
```

