You are tasked with creating a Rust program that simulates a simple RESTful service for managing a collection of books. The program should be able to handle HTTP requests for retrieving all books, adding a new book, updating an existing book, and deleting a book. To achieve this, you need to implement the necessary data structures, HTTP request handling, and book management logic.

Your task is to complete the implementation of the `Book` struct and the `RestfulService` trait, as well as the `main` function to handle HTTP requests using the `actix-web` framework. The `Book` struct should have fields for `id` (a unique identifier for the book), `title`, `author`, and `published_year`. The `RestfulService` trait should define methods for retrieving all books, adding a new book, updating an existing book, and deleting a book.

You should implement the necessary HTTP request handling logic in the `main` function using the `actix-web` framework. The program should listen for incoming HTTP requests on port 8080 and handle requests for the following endpoints:
- GET /books: Retrieve all books
- POST /books: Add a new book
- PUT /books/{id}: Update an existing book
- DELETE /books/{id}: Delete a book by its ID

Your implementation should correctly handle the HTTP requests and interact with the book collection based on the requested operations.

```rust
use actix_web::{web, App, HttpResponse, HttpServer, Responder};
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};

#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize)]
struct Book {
    id: u32,
    title: String,
    author: String,
    published_year: u32,
}

trait RestfulService {
    fn get_all_books(&self) -> Vec<Book>;
    fn add_book(&mut self, book: Book) -> u32;
    fn update_book(&mut self, id: u32, book: Book) -> bool;
    fn delete_book(&mut self, id: u32) -> bool;
}

struct BookCollection {
    books: Arc<Mutex<Vec<Book>>>,
}

impl RestfulService for BookCollection {
    fn get_all_books(&self) -> Vec<Book> {
        self.books.lock().unwrap().clone()
    }

    fn add_book(&mut self, book: Book) -> u32 {
        let mut books = self.books.lock().unwrap();
        let id = books.len() as u32 + 1;
        book.id = id;
        books.push(book);
        id
    }

    fn update_book(&mut self, id: u32, book: Book) -> bool {
        let mut books = self.books.lock().unwrap();
        if let Some(existing_book) = books.iter_mut().find(|b| b.id == id) {
            *existing_book = book;
            true
        } else {
            false
        }
    }

    fn delete_book(&mut self, id: u32) -> bool {
        let mut books = self.books.lock().unwrap();
        if let Some(index) = books.iter().position(|b| b.id == id) {
            books.remove(index);
            true
        } else {
            false
        }
    }
}

async fn get_all_books(data: web::Data<Arc<Mutex<BookCollection>>>) -> impl Responder {
    let book_collection = data.lock().unwrap();
    HttpResponse::Ok().json(book_collection.get_all_books())
}

async fn add_book(
    data: web::Data<Arc<Mutex<BookCollection>>>,
    new_book: web::Json<Book>,
) -> impl Responder {
    let mut book_collection = data.lock().unwrap();
    let id = book_collection.add_book(new_book.into_inner());
    HttpResponse::Created().json(id)
}

async fn update_book(
    data: web::Data<Arc<Mutex<BookCollection>>>,
    path: web::Path<u32>,
    updated_book: web::Json<Book>,
) -> impl Responder {
    let mut book_collection = data.lock().unwrap();
    let id = path.into_inner();
    if book_collection.update_book(id, updated_book.into_inner()) {
        HttpResponse::NoContent().finish()
    } else {
        HttpResponse::NotFound().finish()
    }
}

async fn delete_book(
    data: web::Data<Arc<Mutex<BookCollection>>>,
    path: web::Path<u32>,
) -> impl Responder {
    let mut book_collection = data.lock().unwrap();
    let id = path.into_inner();
    if book_collection.delete_book(id) {
        HttpResponse::NoContent().finish()
    } else {
        HttpResponse::NotFound().finish()
    }
}

#[actix_web::main]
async fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let book_collection = Arc::new(Mutex::new(BookCollection {
        books: Arc::new(Mutex::new(vec![
            Book {
                id: 1,
                title: "The Rust Programming Language".to_string(),
                author: "Steve Klabnik, Carol Nichols".to_string(),
                published_year: 2018,
            },
            Book {
                id: 2,
                title: "Programming Rust".to_string(),
                author: "Jim Blandy, Jason Orendorff".to_string(),
                published_year: 2019,
            },
        ])),
    }));

    HttpServer::new(move || {
        App::new()
            .app_data(web::Data::new(book_collection.clone()))
            .route("/books", web::get().to(get_all_books))
            .route("/books", web::post().to(add_book))
            .route("/books/{id}", web::put().to(update_book))
            .route("/books/{id}", web::delete().to(delete_book))
    })
    .bind("127.0.0.1:8080")?
    .run()
    .await
}
```

