You are tasked with implementing a class to represent a geographic point in a 2D coordinate system. The class should have properties for the unique identifier, azimuth angle, 2D coordinates, and flags indicating whether the azimuth angle is valid and whether the point is a NaN (Not a Number) value.

Your task is to create a C# class `GeographicPoint` that fulfills the following requirements:
- The class should have a private field for the unique identifier `Id` and public read-only property `Id` of type `long`.
- It should have a public read-only property `Azimuth` of type `float` representing the azimuth angle.
- The class should contain a public read-only property `Coordinate` of type `Coordinate2D`, representing the 2D coordinates of the point.
- Include a public read-only property `IsNaN` of type `bool` to indicate whether the point is a NaN value.
- Lastly, the class should have a public read-only property `HasAzimuth` of type `bool` to indicate whether the azimuth angle is valid.

Your task is to implement the `GeographicPoint` class with the specified properties and ensure that the properties are correctly initialized and accessible.

```csharp
public class Coordinate2D
{
    public float X { get; }
    public float Y { get; }

    public Coordinate2D(float x, float y)
    {
        X = x;
        Y = y;
    }
}

public class GeographicPoint
{
    private readonly long _id;
    private readonly float _azimuth;
    private readonly Coordinate2D _coordinate;
    private readonly bool _isNaN;
    private readonly bool _hasAzimuth;

    public long Id => _id;
    public float Azimuth => _azimuth;
    public Coordinate2D Coordinate => _coordinate;
    public bool IsNaN => _isNaN;
    public bool HasAzimuth => _hasAzimuth;

    public GeographicPoint(long id, float azimuth, Coordinate2D coordinate, bool isNaN, bool hasAzimuth)
    {
        _id = id;
        _azimuth = azimuth;
        _coordinate = coordinate;
        _isNaN = isNaN;
        _hasAzimuth = hasAzimuth;
    }
}
```

