def knapsack_max_value(weights, values, capacity):
    n = len(weights)
    cell = [[0] * (capacity + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]

    for i in range(1, n + 1):
        for j in range(1, capacity + 1):
            if weights[i - 1] <= j:
                cell[i][j] = max(cell[i-1][j], values[i - 1] + cell[i - 1][j - weights[i - 1]])
            else:
                cell[i][j] = cell[i - 1][j]

    return cell[n][capacity]
```

The `knapsack_max_value` function initializes a 2D list `cell` to store the maximum value that can be obtained for different capacities and number of items. It then iterates through each item and capacity, calculating the maximum value that can be obtained by either including the current item or excluding it. Finally, it returns the maximum value that can be obtained for the given capacity and items.

