The `transitive_reduce` function takes the adjacency matrix `A` as input and creates a copy `A_red` of the input matrix. It then iterates through all possible pairs of nodes `(i, j)` and a potential intermediate node `k`, and if there is a path from `i` to `k` and from `k` to `j`, it sets `A_red[i][j]` to `False`. Finally, it returns the transitive reduction `A_red` of the input graph.

