using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace Amazon.QLDB.Driver
{
    public class CustomQueueUsingStack
    {
        private Stack<int> inputStack;
        private Stack<int> outputStack;

        public CustomQueueUsingStack()
        {
            inputStack = new Stack<int>();
            outputStack = new Stack<int>();
        }

        public void Enqueue(int value)
        {
            inputStack.Push(value);
        }

        public int Dequeue()
        {
            if (outputStack.Count == 0)
            {
                while (inputStack.Count > 0)
                {
                    outputStack.Push(inputStack.Pop());
                }
            }
            return outputStack.Pop();
        }

        public bool IsEmpty()
        {
            return inputStack.Count == 0 && outputStack.Count == 0;
        }
    }
}
```

In this solution, we create a class `CustomQueueUsingStack` that uses two stacks, `inputStack` and `outputStack`, to simulate the queue operations. The `Enqueue` operation simply pushes the value onto the `inputStack`. The `Dequeue` operation checks if the `outputStack` is empty, and if so, it transfers all elements from the `inputStack` to the `outputStack` in reverse order. Then it pops and returns the top element from the `outputStack`. The `IsEmpty` operation checks if both stacks are empty and returns the result.

