You are working on a project that involves processing data using the PyTorch library in C++. As part of the project, you need to implement a function that takes a vector of pairs and returns two torch tensors. Each pair in the input vector consists of an index (integer) and a distance (float). The function should stack all the indices and distances separately into torch tensors and return them as a pair.

You are given the following code snippet as a starting point:

```cpp
#include <torch/torch.h>
#include <vector>

std::pair<torch::Tensor, torch::Tensor> process_data(const std::vector<std::pair<int, float>>& data) {
    std::vector<torch::Tensor> batch_idx;
    std::vector<torch::Tensor> batch_dist;

    for (const auto& out_pair : data) {
        batch_idx.push_back(torch::tensor(out_pair.first));
        batch_dist.push_back(torch::tensor(out_pair.second));
    }
    auto out_idx = torch::stack(batch_idx);
    auto out_dist = torch::stack(batch_dist);
    return std::make_pair(out_idx, out_dist);
}
```

