        String url = innerApiUrl + "/api/pay/createpayrecordapp.do?payType=" + payType + "&payID=" + encodedPayID + "&payNumber=" + payNumber + "&payMoney=" + payMoney + "&payChannel=" + payChannel + "&payTime=" + encodedPayTime + "&payOrder=" + payOrder;
        return url;
    }

    private String urlEncode(String input) {
        try {
            return URLEncoder.encode(input, "UTF-8")
                    .replaceAll("\\+", "%20")
                    .replaceAll("\\%21", "!")
                    .replaceAll("\\%27", "'")
                    .replaceAll("\\%28", "(")
                    .replaceAll("\\%29", ")")
                    .replaceAll("\\%7E", "~");
        } catch (UnsupportedEncodingException e) {
            // Handle encoding exception
            return input; // Return original input in case of exception
        }
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `createpayrecordapp` method constructs the URL using the provided parameters and the inner API URL. It also encodes the `payID` and `payTime` using the `urlEncode` method, which replaces special characters with their corresponding URL-encoded values. The `urlEncode` method handles the URL encoding and replaces additional characters to ensure proper encoding. If an encoding exception occurs, the original input is returned.

