You are tasked with creating a program to manage a library's book inventory. The program should allow users to add new books, remove existing books, and display the current list of books in the inventory. Each book in the inventory should have a unique identifier, title, author, and quantity.

Your task is to implement the `BookInventory` class, which should have the following functionalities:
1. `addBook`: A method to add a new book to the inventory. If the book already exists, the quantity should be incremented.
2. `removeBook`: A method to remove a book from the inventory. If the book's quantity becomes zero, it should be completely removed from the inventory.
3. `displayInventory`: A method to display the current list of books in the inventory, including their unique identifiers, titles, authors, and quantities.

You should also create a simple user interface using the provided code snippet as a reference. The user interface should have text boxes and buttons to allow users to input book details and perform the specified operations on the book inventory.

Your task is to complete the implementation of the `BookInventory` class and create a user interface that integrates with the class to provide the required functionalities.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace LibraryInventoryManagement
{
    public class Book
    {
        public int Id { get; set; }
        public string Title { get; set; }
        public string Author { get; set; }
        public int Quantity { get; set; }
    }

    public class BookInventory
    {
        private List<Book> inventory;

        public BookInventory()
        {
            inventory = new List<Book>();
        }

        public void addBook(int id, string title, string author, int quantity)
        {
            Book existingBook = inventory.Find(b => b.Id == id);
            if (existingBook != null)
            {
                existingBook.Quantity += quantity;
            }
            else
            {
                inventory.Add(new Book { Id = id, Title = title, Author = author, Quantity = quantity });
            }
        }

        public void removeBook(int id)
        {
            Book bookToRemove = inventory.Find(b => b.Id == id);
            if (bookToRemove != null)
            {
                if (bookToRemove.Quantity > 1)
                {
                    bookToRemove.Quantity--;
                }
                else
                {
                    inventory.Remove(bookToRemove);
                }
            }
        }

        public void displayInventory()
        {
            foreach (var book in inventory)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"ID: {book.Id}, Title: {book.Title}, Author: {book.Author}, Quantity: {book.Quantity}");
            }
        }
    }

    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            BookInventory libraryInventory = new BookInventory();

            // Example usage
            libraryInventory.addBook(1, "The Great Gatsby", "F. Scott Fitzgerald", 5);
            libraryInventory.addBook(2, "To Kill a Mockingbird", "Harper Lee", 3);
            libraryInventory.addBook(1, "The Great Gatsby", "F. Scott Fitzgerald", 2);
            libraryInventory.removeBook(2);
            libraryInventory.displayInventory();
        }
    }
}
```

