You are tasked with implementing a function that can efficiently determine the namespace of a given C++ code snippet. The namespace is a C++ feature that allows organizing code elements into a named scope. Your function should take a string representing a C++ code snippet as input and return the namespace(s) present in the code.

Your task is to implement the function `findNamespace` that takes a string `code` as input and returns a vector of strings representing the namespace(s) present in the code. The input `code` will be a valid C++ code snippet. The function should handle nested namespaces and should return the namespaces in the order they appear in the code.

Example:
For the input code:
```
namespace clblast {
  namespace utils {
    // Code here
  }
}
```
The function should return `{"clblast", "utils"}`.

output:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <string>
#include <regex>

std::vector<std::string> findNamespace(const std::string& code) {
    std::vector<std::string> namespaces;
    std::regex namespaceRegex(R"(namespace\s+(\w+)\s*\{)");

    auto words_begin = std::sregex_iterator(code.begin(), code.end(), namespaceRegex);
    auto words_end = std::sregex_iterator();

    for (std::sregex_iterator i = words_begin; i != words_end; ++i) {
        std::smatch match = *i;
        namespaces.push_back(match[1].str());
    }

    return namespaces;
}

int main() {
    std::string code = R"(
        namespace clblast {
          namespace utils {
            // Code here
          }
        }
    )";

    std::vector<std::string> result = findNamespace(code);
    for (const auto& ns : result) {
        std::cout << ns << std::endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

The `findNamespace` function uses regular expressions to search for namespace declarations in the input code. It iterates through the matches and extracts the namespace names, storing them in a vector. The main function demonstrates the usage of `findNamespace` with a sample code snippet and prints the extracted namespaces.

