Your task is to implement the `AttributeManager` class with the following specifications:

1. The class should have a constructor that takes an object as a parameter and uses reflection to initialize the object's attributes.
2. Implement a method `setAttribute($attributeName, $value)` that sets the value of the specified attribute.
3. Implement a method `getAttribute($attributeName)` that returns the value of the specified attribute.
4. Implement a method `hasAttribute($attributeName)` that returns true if the specified attribute exists, and false otherwise.

Your implementation should use the `ReflectionObject` and `ReflectionProperty` classes for introspection.

```php
class AttributeManager {
    private $object;
    private $reflectionObject;

    public function __construct($object) {
        $this->object = $object;
        $this->reflectionObject = new ReflectionObject($object);
    }

    public function setAttribute($attributeName, $value) {
        $reflectionProperty = $this->_getReflectionProperty($attributeName);
        if ($reflectionProperty instanceof ReflectionProperty) {
            $reflectionProperty->setValue($this->object, $value);
        }
    }

    public function getAttribute($attributeName) {
        $reflectionProperty = $this->_getReflectionProperty($attributeName);
        if ($reflectionProperty instanceof ReflectionProperty) {
            return $reflectionProperty->getValue($this->object);
        }
        return null;
    }

    public function hasAttribute($attributeName) {
        $reflectionProperty = $this->_getReflectionProperty($attributeName);
        return $reflectionProperty instanceof ReflectionProperty;
    }

    private function _getReflectionProperty($attributeName) {
        return $this->reflectionObject->getProperty($attributeName);
    }
}
```

