```csharp
public static class BSTExtensions
{
    public static Node DestroySubtree(this Node root, int target)
    {
        if (root == null)
        {
            return null;
        }
        if (target < root.Data)
        {
            root.Left = DestroySubtree(root.Left, target);
        }
        else if (target > root.Data)
        {
            root.Right = DestroySubtree(root.Right, target);
        }
        else
        {
            root.Left = null;
            root.Right = null;
            root = null;
        }
        return root;
    }
}
```

The `DestroySubtree` method first checks if the current node is null, in which case it returns null. Then, it recursively traverses the BST to find the node with data equal to the target value. Once found, it sets the left and right children of the node to null and then sets the node itself to null. Finally, it returns the modified BST after removing the subtree.

