You are tasked with implementing a generic class for managing entity properties in a C# application. The class should support properties with change tracking functionality. Your task is to create a generic class `EntityProperty<T>` that encapsulates a property value and provides change tracking functionality using the `SetField` method. The `SetField` method should compare the new value with the existing value and update the property only if the new value is different. Additionally, the class should provide a method to reset the property to its original value.

Your `EntityProperty<T>` class should have the following structure:
```csharp
public class EntityProperty<T>
{
    private T _value;
    private T _originalValue;
    private bool _isDirty;

    public EntityProperty(T value)
    {
        _value = value;
        _originalValue = value;
        _isDirty = false;
    }

    public T Value
    {
        get { return _value; }
        set { SetField(ref _value, value); }
    }

    public bool IsDirty
    {
        get { return _isDirty; }
    }

    public void Reset()
    {
        _value = _originalValue;
        _isDirty = false;
    }

    private void SetField(ref T field, T value)
    {
        if (!EqualityComparer<T>.Default.Equals(field, value))
        {
            field = value;
            _isDirty = true;
        }
    }
}
```

