You are tasked with implementing a function to reverse the order of migrations in a Laravel migration file. In Laravel, migrations are used to modify the database schema and are typically stored in the `database/migrations` directory. Each migration file contains an `up` method to apply the migration and a corresponding `down` method to reverse it.

Your task is to create a function `reverseMigrations` that takes a string representing the content of a migration file as input and returns the content with the order of migrations reversed. The input string will be in the following format:

```php
<?php

use Illuminate\Database\Migrations\Migration;
use Illuminate\Database\Schema\Blueprint;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Schema;

class CreateExampleTable extends Migration
{
    public function up()
    {
        Schema::create('example', function (Blueprint $table) {
            $table->id();
            $table->string('name');
            $table->timestamps();
        });
    }

    public function down()
    {
        Schema::dropIfExists('example');
    }
}
```

The `up` method contains the code to apply the migration, while the `down` method contains the code to reverse the migration. Your task is to reverse the order of these methods in the input string, such that the `down` method appears before the `up` method in the returned string.

Function Signature: `function reverseMigrations(string $input): string`

Example:
Input:
```php
<?php

use Illuminate\Database\Migrations\Migration;
use Illuminate\Database\Schema\Blueprint;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Schema;

class CreateExampleTable extends Migration
{
    public function up()
    {
        Schema::create('example', function (Blueprint $table) {
            $table->id();
            $table->string('name');
            $table->timestamps();
        });
    }

    public function down()
    {
        Schema::dropIfExists('example');
    }
}
```
Output:
```php
<?php

use Illuminate\Database\Migrations\Migration;
use Illuminate\Database\Schema\Blueprint;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Schema;

class CreateExampleTable extends Migration
{
    public function down()
    {
        Schema::dropIfExists('example');
    }

    public function up()
    {
        Schema::create('example', function (Blueprint $table) {
            $table->id();
            $table->string('name');
            $table->timestamps();
        });
    }
}
```

output:
```php
function reverseMigrations(string $input): string {
    $upIndex = strpos($input, 'public function up()');
    $downIndex = strpos($input, 'public function down()');

    if ($upIndex !== false && $downIndex !== false) {
        $upMethod = substr($input, $upIndex, $downIndex - $upIndex);
        $downMethod = substr($input, $downIndex);

        $reversedContent = str_replace($upMethod, '', $input);
        $reversedContent = str_replace($downMethod, '', $reversedContent);

        $reversedContent = str_replace('}', '', $reversedContent);
        $reversedContent = rtrim($reversedContent, "\n");
        $reversedContent .= $downMethod . $upMethod . "}\n}";

        return $reversedContent;
    }

    return $input; // Return original input if up and down methods are not found
}
```

