```java
import java.util.Stack;

public class ExpressionTreeParser {
    /**
     * Returns an ExpressionTree based off the input text
     * @throws InvalidCommandException 
     */
    private Command createExpressionTree(CommandParser lang, String[] text) throws InvalidCommandException {
        CommandList root = myFactory.newCommandList();
        boolean parsingGroup = false;
        boolean firstArgInGroup = false;

        Stack<Command> currCommands = new Stack<Command>();
        currCommands.push(root);

        for (String token : text) {
            if (token.equals("(")) {
                parsingGroup = true;
                firstArgInGroup = true;
            } else if (token.equals(")")) {
                parsingGroup = false;
                firstArgInGroup = false;
                // Handle closing of group and update the expression tree
                // Pop the current command and update the tree structure
                currCommands.pop();
            } else {
                if (parsingGroup) {
                    if (firstArgInGroup) {
                        // Handle the first argument in the group
                        // Create a new command based on the token and add it to the current command
                        Command newCommand = lang.parseCommand(token);
                        currCommands.peek().add(newCommand);
                        firstArgInGroup = false;
                    } else {
                        // Handle subsequent arguments in the group
                        // Create a new command based on the token and add it to the current command
                        Command newCommand = lang.parseCommand(token);
                        currCommands.peek().add(newCommand);
                    }
                } else {
                    // Handle non-group tokens
                    // Create a new command based on the token and add it to the current command
                    Command newCommand = lang.parseCommand(token);
                    currCommands.peek().add(newCommand);
                }
            }
        }

        if (parsingGroup) {
            // Throw an exception if the input text ends with an unclosed group
            throw new InvalidCommandException("Unclosed group in the input text");
        }

        // Return the root of the expression tree
        return root;
    }
}
```
In the solution, the `createExpressionTree` method iterates through the input text tokens and handles the parsing of groups and their arguments. It uses a stack to keep track of the current commands while building the expression tree. The method creates new commands based on the tokens and adds them to the current command or updates the tree structure when a group is closed. It also throws an exception if the input text ends with an unclosed group. Finally, it returns the root of the expression tree.

