class Solution(object):
    def lowestCommonAncestor(self, root, p, q):
        """
        :type root: TreeNode
        :type p: TreeNode
        :type q: TreeNode
        :rtype: TreeNode
        """
        while root:
            if p.val < root.val and q.val < root.val:
                root = root.left
            elif p.val > root.val and q.val > root.val:
                root = root.right
            else:
                return root
```

The provided solution implements the `lowestCommonAncestor` method using the binary search tree property. It iterates through the tree, comparing the values of the nodes `p` and `q` with the value of the current root node to determine the lowest common ancestor. If the values of `p` and `q` are on different sides of the current root node, the current root node is the lowest common ancestor, and it is returned. If not, the iteration continues in the appropriate subtree until the lowest common ancestor is found.

