Your task is to implement the function `search_functions` that takes in the directory path and a boolean flag indicating whether to match imported functions. The function should search for functions within shared libraries in the specified directory and return a list of function names that match the criteria.

The shared libraries are files with the extension ".so" and contain function symbols that can be either imported or exported. If the `imported` flag is set to true, the function should only return the names of imported functions. If the flag is set to false, the function should return the names of exported functions.

You should use the `goblin` crate to parse the shared libraries and extract the function symbols. The `goblin` crate provides facilities for parsing and working with binary formats, including shared libraries.

You are provided with the following code snippet as a starting point:

```rust
use std::path::PathBuf;
use structopt::StructOpt;

/// Command-line options
#[derive(StructOpt)]
struct Opt {
    /// Directory to search in
    #[structopt(short, long, default_value = "/lib")]
    dir: PathBuf,

    /// Match imported instead of exported functions
    #[structopt(short, long)]
    imported: bool,
}

fn main() {
    // Process arguments
    let opt = Opt::from_args();
    // Call search_functions with opt.dir and opt.imported
}

fn search_functions(dir: &PathBuf, imported: bool) -> Vec<String> {
    // Implement the search logic using the goblin crate
    // Return the list of function names that match the criteria
}
```

output:
```rust
use std::path::PathBuf;
use goblin::Object;
use std::fs;
use std::io;

fn search_functions(dir: &PathBuf, imported: bool) -> Vec<String> {
    let mut result = Vec::new();

    // Read the directory and filter for shared libraries
    if let Ok(entries) = fs::read_dir(dir) {
        for entry in entries {
            if let Ok(entry) = entry {
                if let Ok(metadata) = entry.metadata() {
                    if metadata.is_file() {
                        if let Some(extension) = entry.path().extension() {
                            if extension == "so" {
                                // Parse the shared library using goblin
                                if let Ok(data) = fs::read(entry.path()) {
                                    if let Ok(object) = Object::parse(&data) {
                                        // Extract function symbols based on imported flag
                                        if let Some(symbols) = object.dynamic_symbols() {
                                            for symbol in symbols {
                                                if imported {
                                                    if symbol.is_import() {
                                                        if let Some(name) = symbol.name {
                                                            result.push(name.to_string());
                                                        }
                                                    }
                                                } else {
                                                    if symbol.is_export() {
                                                        if let Some(name) = symbol.name {
                                                            result.push(name.to_string());
                                                        }
                                                    }
                                                }
                                            }
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    result
}
```

This solution implements the `search_functions` function to search for function names within shared libraries based on the specified directory and the imported flag. It uses the `goblin` crate to parse the shared libraries and extract the function symbols. The function iterates through the shared library files, parses them using `goblin`, and filters the function symbols based on the imported flag, adding the matching function names to the result vector.

