namespace SOFe\AwaitStd;

use Exception;

final class PromiseRejectedException extends Exception {}

class Promise {
    private $state;
    private $value;
    private $onFulfilled;
    private $onRejected;

    public function __construct(callable $executor) {
        $this->state = 'pending';
        $this->value = null;
        $this->onFulfilled = null;
        $this->onRejected = null;

        $resolve = function ($value) {
            if ($this->state === 'pending') {
                $this->state = 'fulfilled';
                $this->value = $value;
                if ($this->onFulfilled) {
                    $onFulfilled = $this->onFulfilled;
                    $onFulfilled($this->value);
                }
            }
        };

        $reject = function ($reason) {
            if ($this->state === 'pending') {
                $this->state = 'rejected';
                $this->value = $reason;
                if ($this->onRejected) {
                    $onRejected = $this->onRejected;
                    $onRejected($this->value);
                }
            }
        };

        try {
            $executor($resolve, $reject);
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            $reject($e);
        }
    }

    public function then(callable $onFulfilled, callable $onRejected = null) {
        if ($this->state === 'fulfilled') {
            $onFulfilled($this->value);
        } elseif ($this->state === 'rejected' && $onRejected) {
            $onRejected($this->value);
        } else {
            $this->onFulfilled = $onFulfilled;
            $this->onRejected = $onRejected;
        }
    }

    public function catch(callable $onRejected) {
        if ($this->state === 'rejected') {
            $onRejected($this->value);
        } else {
            $this->onRejected = $onRejected;
        }
    }
}
```

This implementation of the Promise class adheres to the specified requirements. It handles asynchronous operations, resolves and rejects promises, and executes the appropriate callbacks when the promise is fulfilled or rejected. The then and catch methods allow for handling the promise's resolution or rejection in a clean and organized manner.

