You are tasked with creating a Rust program that models a simple file registry system. The program should define a FileType enum and implement functionality to register and retrieve file types using a registry module. The FileType enum should represent different types of files, and the registry module should provide methods to register and retrieve file types.

Your task is to complete the implementation of the FileType enum and the registry module. The FileType enum should have variants for different file types, and the registry module should provide methods to register and retrieve file types.

Complete the following tasks:
1. Define the FileType enum with variants for Image, Text, and Binary file types.
2. Implement the register_file_type function in the registry module, which takes a FileType and registers it in the file registry.
3. Implement the get_file_type function in the registry module, which takes a file name and returns the FileType if it is registered, or None if it is not registered.

Use the given code snippet as a starting point and complete the program to achieve the desired functionality.

```rust
pub use self::registry::*;
pub use self::target::*;

pub mod registry;
pub mod target;

/// Specifies a file type.
/// Analgous to `llvm::CodeGenFileType`
#[repr(C)]
pub enum FileType {
    // Define the variants for different file types
    Image,
    Text,
    Binary,
}
```

output:
```rust
// registry.rs
use std::collections::HashMap;

pub struct FileRegistry {
    file_types: HashMap<String, FileType>,
}

impl FileRegistry {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        FileRegistry {
            file_types: HashMap::new(),
        }
    }

    pub fn register_file_type(&mut self, file_name: String, file_type: FileType) {
        self.file_types.insert(file_name, file_type);
    }

    pub fn get_file_type(&self, file_name: &str) -> Option<&FileType> {
        self.file_types.get(file_name)
    }
}

// main.rs
use registry::FileRegistry;

fn main() {
    let mut file_registry = FileRegistry::new();

    file_registry.register_file_type("image.png".to_string(), FileType::Image);
    file_registry.register_file_type("document.txt".to_string(), FileType::Text);
    file_registry.register_file_type("data.bin".to_string(), FileType::Binary);

    let file_type = file_registry.get_file_type("image.png");
    match file_type {
        Some(ft) => println!("File type: {:?}", ft),
        None => println!("File type not found"),
    }
}
```

