class MyClass:
    def __init__(self):
        self._friendCache = {}

    def __getattr__(self, attr):
        if attr.startswith('friend_'):
            if attr not in self._friendCache:
                method = getattr(self, attr, None)
                if callable(method):
                    self._friendCache[attr] = method
                else:
                    raise AttributeError(f"'{type(self).__name__}' object has no attribute '{attr}'")
            return self._friendCache[attr]
        else:
            raise AttributeError(f"'{type(self).__name__}' object has no attribute '{attr}'")
```

In the solution, the `__getattr__` method is modified to check if the accessed attribute starts with "friend_". If it does, the method is cached in the `self._friendCache` dictionary. Subsequent accesses to the same method will return it from the cache. If the attribute does not start with "friend_", an AttributeError is raised to maintain the default behavior of `__getattr__`.

